    "answer": {
      "short": "Team A: minimum $19$, $Q_1=23$, median $26$, $Q_3=27$, maximum $28$ goals. Team B has the higher median ($27$ versus $26$). Team A is more consistent: IQR $4$ versus $7$ goals and range $9$ versus $14$ goals. Team A is negatively skewed; Team B is approximately symmetric or slightly positively skewed.",
      "worked": "There are $15$ scores. The median is the 8th score; the lower and upper quartiles are the 4th and 12th scores.\n\nThe cumulative count through $24$ goals is $1+0+1+1+1+3=7$, so the 8th score is $26$. The 4th score is $23$ and the 12th score is $27$.\n\nTeam A's five-number summary is $19,\\ 23,\\ 26,\\ 27,\\ 28$ goals. Alternatively, use a calculator to find this summary. Construct the box from $23$ to $27$, mark the median at $26$, and draw whiskers to $19$ and $28$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\mathrm{IQR}_A&=27-23\\\\&=4\\text{ goals}\\\\\\mathrm{IQR}_B&=31-24\\\\&=7\\text{ goals}\\\\\\mathrm{Range}_A&=28-19\\\\&=9\\text{ goals}\\\\\\mathrm{Range}_B&=35-21\\\\&=14\\text{ goals}\\end{align*}$$\n\nTeam B generally scores more goals per game because its median is higher: $27$ compared with $26$. Team A is more consistent because both its IQR and range are smaller. Team A is negatively skewed, with a longer lower whisker and lower half of the box. Team B is approximately symmetric or slightly positively skewed.",
